result.strongest_argument:
Stage 0 has no component, and no measured quantity, without a published counterpart. The proposal's one remaining novelty claim ("the combination has no direct prior", Novelty verdict NO_DIRECT_PRIOR_FOUND) therefore describes a trivial recombination, not a novelty delta.

(1) The measurement framework is Measuring the Checker (MtC, 2609.22220), ported to Triton. MtC already has every one of these pieces:
- deterministic rules in six families;
- compiled-image deduplication (the GPU form of Trivial Compiler Equivalence) and crash quarantine;
- a witnessed denominator with validity-gated inputs, the gate that drops inputs on which the fp32 reference leaves fp64 tolerance;
- per-family miss rates;
- a per-problem 50/50 id-hash dev/test split;
- greedy set cover over the kill matrix, which Stage 0 calls c-lite (registration 5.5);
- an audit of KBV that splits its gain into inputs and tolerance (Stage 0's c@1e-3 vs c@1e-2 ablation);
- a count of false rejections of correct kernels by a hardened protocol (107 false kills).

The project's own `harness/q1/mutate/README.md` says the taxonomy "ports Measuring the Checker ... from CUDA to Triton". Registration 15.3 says the split "mirrors the paper's per-problem id-hash holdout". Prediction 13.2 says Stage 0 "replicates MtC section 2 on Triton".

(2) Each rung reimplements a named published check: (a) is KernelBench, (b) is KernelGYM/Dr. Kernel, c1 is KBV, c2 follows robust-kbench. MtC already scores a ladder of protocols on one denominator (official, KBV at 1e-2, fuzz, KBV at 1e-3).

(3) The "independent audit as reference standard" with tolerance-free contracts is the Contract-Grade Verifier's (CGV, 2608.12700) design:
- twelve contract gates, several tolerance-free, against a full-precision reference;
- a two-sided red team of 19 deliberately broken kernels (input return, caching, fp16 accumulation, nondeterminism, one-shape-only) plus a positive control;
- 98.5% fidelity agreement with KernelBench's own harness (Stage 0's criterion 1);
- the differential "standard test vs audit", 1,487 against 14, which is gate (a)'s FAR and FRR against an audit.

A5 reimplements lethe outright. Sarkar's Correctness Illusion and its companions (2606.20128, 2606.27396, 2607.16228) already put correctness checkers for Triton kernels against an fp64 reference with boundary shapes, on correct controls and seeded bugs. They report each strategy's recall next to its control false-positive rate (boundary shapes 78% recall at 0/128 FP; calibrated tolerance 82.4% recall at 20/1,882 FP) and time-to-first-failure. That is the two-sided "FAR and FRR per checker, with cost" design.

(4) Every control kind comes from a published hack catalog: Dr. Kernel Fig. 2 decoys, KBV App. H.1 identity shortcuts, lethe returns_cached / buffer_aliasing / shape_specific, and KernelBench's adversarial kernels (copied verbatim).

(5) Only three deltas remain, and none is a new mechanism:
- substrate origin (TorchInductor and pre-2025 human Triton instead of LLM-written CUDA) is a port;
- FRR over at least 72 independent units is a difference of scale, not of kind;
- the launch-path rung is uninformative on mutants by construction (proposal F3 and K-I4).

(6) On the mutant arm MtC strictly dominates: about 155 pooled witnessed test mutants against 7,384 (1/48), for a projected 20-25 GPU-h against MtC's about 30 GPU-h. Blind discrimination should therefore find the prior strictly dominant on the shared mechanism, and Novelty is capped at 74.

(7) The audit-as-ground-truth delta the proposal defends (confidence 0.45) is defeated under the registered policy by F1. F1 itself is not new: it is MtC's tolerance vacuity (an all-zeros output passes once the blind band is wide enough), combined with MtC's unrefereeable references against fp64 and the cancellation-prone-normaliser pathology in Calibrating the Checksum (2610.02240 section 2.3, max-to-median ratio 389). Even this wave's own negative result (Negative-Result Value item 4) is therefore a known mechanism. A further delta is partly occupied by MtC itself: MtC's rule `output-elements-one-extra-lane` is killed by "a misaligned output plus a CUDA memory checker". The memory-checker witness the proposal credits to A4 against MtC is therefore not exclusive to Stage 0.
